{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"26f3cb136d0366e2592a5fd8be2e771a38eed2c883348bfeb2bdfead6fb199f2","digest":{"component_or_area":"criteria eval CLI — dual-gate id resolution","key_entities":["src/rebar/_cli/_llm_eval_commands.py","src/rebar/llm/code_review/registry.py","code_review.registry.effective_criteria()","plan_review.registry.by_id()","project.foo","calibrate_criterion","tests/unit/test_code_review_project_criteria.py"],"problem_keywords":["criteria eval CLI","code-review ids","plan-review registry","dual-registry admission","gate resolution","ambiguity detection"],"propositions":["The criteria eval CLI preflight rejects project code-review ids as unknown because it only checks plan_review.registry.by_id(), never reaching the gate-aware eval resolver.","The preflight must admit ids present in exactly one of {plan_review, code_review} registry and resolve to that gate deterministically for dispatch to calibrate_criterion.","An id active in both registries must be rejected as ambiguous with a diagnostic message naming both gates; an id in neither must retain the existing unknown error.","The subparser help text must include the concrete code-review example project.foo alongside the plan-review example to document the dual-gate capability."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787727420992897001,"uuid":"ffc75e60-0a61-4513-b21d-d0179833b2a7"}